 ## Background
-Tricubic interpolation is a standard extension of cubic Hermite interpolation to three dimensions. It is widely used in medical imaging and scientific visualization for upsampling 3D volumes where smoothness is critical [S2]. The method was highlighted in game development contexts (e.g., Irradiance Volumes) for its efficiency in approximating smooth lighting fields using samples and gradients [S3, unofficial].
